<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Madra Kingdom</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chennai">Madras</a> were an ancient people of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a> in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, named in Vedic texts, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahabharata">Mahabharata</a> and Buddhist sources, with their capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sagala">Sakala</a>, modern Sialkot. In the epic, Madri, the wife of Pandu, and her brother Shalya are Madras. Buddhist tradition records that King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bimbisara">Bimbisara of Magadha</a> took a Madra princess, Khema, as one of his wives.</p></div>
